Sonarqube Document:
Android Sonarqube Project:
Steps:
1)We have to make service Connection between Pipeline and Sonarqube dashboard.

2)Get the project name and project key from Devops Team.
3)Get the Credentials like username and password of the sonarqube dashboard.
4)Get the required details from Developers.
• What is the code they are using
• What are the plugin tools they are using and their version
• What is the OS machine and Version they are using
• What is the coverage xmlReportPaths they are using
• What are the coverage exclusion they are using
• What are the test results file they are using
5)In Android project we are using Gradle Tool and Jacoco coverage Tool for Sonarqube.
6)Start building the soanrqube .yml pipeline with all the required details.
7)We have to use Prepare Analysis Task in Pipeline.

task: SonarQubePrepare@4
inputs:
SonarQube: 'sonarqube-subway-mob-android'
scannerMode: 'Other'
projectKey: 'Guest-MobileApps_subway-mob-android'
extraProperties: |
sonar.projectName=subway-mob-android
sonar.projectKey=Guest-MobileApps_subway-mob-android
sonar.java.coveragePlugin=jacoco
sonar.coverage.jacoco.xmlReportPaths=testUatRealDebugUnitTestCoverage.xml
sonar.exclusions=
sonar.coverage.exclusions=
8)Run the gradle task for sonarqube and publish the junit results.

task: Gradle@2
displayName: 'gradlew assembleuatRealRelease'
inputs:
gradleWrapperFile: 'gradlew'
gradleOptions: '-Xmx3072m'
tasks: 'testUatRealDebugUnitTestCoverage'
publishJUnitResults: true
testResultsFiles: '$(System.DefaultWorkingDirectory)//test-results//*.xml'
javaHomeOption: 'JDKVersion'
jdkVersionOption: '1.11'
jdkArchitectureOption: 'x64'
sonarQubeRunAnalysis: true
sqGradlePluginVersionChoice: 'build'
spotBugsAnalysis: false
